            <ArticleTitle>Development of potent μ and δ opioid agonists with high lipophilicity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>382-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/jm100982d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An SAR study on the Dmt-substituted enkephalin-like tetrapeptide with a N-phenyl-N-piperidin-4-ylpropionamide moiety at the C-terminal was performed and has resulted in highly potent ligands at μ and δ opioid receptors. In general, ligands with the substitution of D-Nle(2) and halogenation of the aromatic ring of Phe(4) showed highly increased opioid activities. Ligand 6 with good biological activities in vitro demonstrated potent in vivo antihyperalgesic and antiallodynic effects in the tail-flick assay.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
